    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` feature so newly created owners are assigned a code formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**What the code does:** On owner creation, the prefix is the upper-cased first three letters of the last name, and `NNNN` is a zero-padded 4-digit global sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\n**Changes, each kept in its proper layer:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in SQL).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so it's serialized on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up).\n\n4. **`CustomerCodeGenerator.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility component that formats `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` given a last name and sequence number, safely handling last names shorter than three letters.\n\n5. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 the create path (which owns the repository) computes the sequence as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` and delegates formatting to the generator, only for new owners without a code (so updates never reassign). The JPQL count auto-flushes pending inserts, making the sequence strictly increasing across creates.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 explicitly ignores `customerCode` on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping since it's server-assigned, not client-supplied; the `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` direction maps it automatically by name.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the build is green.",
